From: ae-automation-bot <ae-automation-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 22:57:05 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 390/443] [ae-patch] Fix the review findings on 0389: prune on
 a failed ownership check, stop on a failed root re-read, close the archive
 and side chat race

A failed read or ownership check on a side chat now prunes its subtree; only a
write failure after ownership was established walks on. A failed re-read of
the archived root stops the walk. The fork route re-reads the source after a
side chat is committed and, when the source is archived by then, archives the
new side chat under the same root, stops it and refuses the request, which
closes the window between the pre-check and the archive cascade. The refusal
now runs before the agent-binding check.
